"""Fish part 1: the schools of fish (game/fish.cpp) against the original's (script/fs_diff.cpp, suite fish). Run: on
script/build_fs.bat, the full 1,500 cases; MUT_HARNESS script, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and fs_calls.s,
MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS "fs_diff: .*, N checks, 0 failures".

482 mutants, 68 not building; 375 of the 414 building killed at first, 380 after the test was widened (the camera 1.1 m
from the first fish, a scene without a camera, an entry after the made saves, the reader's depth after the loads). The
34 left:
- The port's fixes: a model without its "ryba" frame makes no fish (209 num: the original calls through null, not
  given).
- Leaks, not observed: the fish not deleted (262 del).
- Not given: a chunk with 1 byte left (158 num); a direction or velocity chunk too short (161 num; 185 num); a short
  speed chunk left standing (156 num; 156 arith: its header's bits are a denormal the original steps with the FPU's
  wider exponent; the made saves follow it with a whole one).
- Not compared: the fish's place's w (224 num: a stale local in the original).
- Float boundaries not reached: a square exactly 1e-8 (60 cmp; 73 cmp); a square exactly 1 taken as 1.5 (64 num); the
  step exactly the distance (383 cmp); a fish exactly 1 m from its target (437 num); the camera exactly 1 m^2 from a
  fish (463 cmp).
- Equivalent: a float within 1e-8 of 1 is 1 (62 cmp; 71 cmp; 62 arith; 71 arith: no square is -1); squares exactly
  1.5 (62 num; 71 num); a non-zero component's sign (77 cmp; 79 cmp); a direction's y of exactly 0 levelled the same
  either way (355 cmp; 357 cmp; 359 cmp; 359 num; 361 cmp); the slide's end and normal filled on a hit (365 num; 366
  num); the step the same when it equals the length (439 cmp); the flag set by the getter (446 bool); the id set by the
  Descend that works (152 num); without the first Descend the loop enters the 9999 chunk itself, the closing Ascend
  leaving it the same (153 del); the creator's registration answer unused (482 bool)."""
